Z||000001||Standard||03-25-2001||06:19 PM||||215/60HR-15<P>215 = section width<BR>60  = height of sidewall as % of section       width<BR>H   = speed rating<BR>R   = Radial tire<BR>15  = Rim diameter<P>S = 112 MPH<BR>T = 118 MPH<BR>U = 124 MPH<BR>H = 130 MPH<BR>V = 149 MPH<BR>W = 168 MPH<BR>Y = 186 MPH<BR>Z = 186+ MPH<P>For tires having a maximum speed capability above 149 mph, a Z <I>may</I> appear in the size designation.  For tires having a maximum speed capability above 186 mph, a Z <I>must</I> appear in the size designation.<P>Fiero's came with H rated tires.<P>Hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons :D||||reg||1
